The earliest and most famous MOF with ${\sf M}_{2}({\sf C O O})_{4}$ clusters is HKUST-1 (Hong Kong University of Science and Technology-1) reported by Williams et al.[74] Its metal nodes are composed of binuclear $\mathsf{C u}^{2+}$ and four groups of COO- to form binuclear paddle metal cluster ${\mathsf{C u}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}$ . Two $\mathsf{C u}^{2+}$ of ${\mathsf{C u}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}$ are usually coordinated by solvent molecules in the axial direction, giving a tetragonal cone coordination configuration. The axial coordination solvent molecules can be removed by simple heating activation, thus exposing the unsaturated metal sites and exhibiting the Lewis acid catalytic activity. The strong Lewis acidity of ${\mathsf{C u}}^{2+}$ encourages researchers to investigate the performance of corresponding MOFs. For example, Zhao and coworkers[75] synthesized a nitrogen-rich triazole group functional MOF $\mathsf{i C u}_{4}[(\mathsf{C}_{57}\mathsf{H}_{32}\mathsf{N}_{12})(\mathsf{C O O})_{8}]\}_{\mathsf{n}}$ by using ${\mathsf{C u}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}$ cluster as a building block (Figure 3). It showed excellent catalytic performance. The ield of cycloaddition by ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ with propylene oxide can reach $96\%$ . Interestingly, the synthesized MOF exhibits high size selectivity toward different substrates, and its activity showed a sharp decrease when using the larger reactant molecules. They concluded that high activity of the catalyst can due to incorporating both exposed metal sites and nitrogen-rich triazole groups.
After that, Zhu group[76] reported a novel MOF JUC-1000, hich was constructed by reacting 2,4-bis(3,5-dicarboxyphenylamino)-6-ol triazine with ${\mathsf{C u}}({\mathsf{N O}}_{3})_{2}$ to form ${\mathsf{C u}}_{2}({\mathsf{C O O}})_{4}$ cluster based MOF (Figure 4). JUC-1000 exhibited fficient catalytic performance for the cycloaddition of propylene oxide and ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ to form propylene carbonate under mild conditions. They suggested that polar groups such as -OH and -NH on the ligands and $\mathsf{C u}^{2+}$ in JUC-1000 synergistically activate the epoxides, thus significantly enhancing the reaction activity. Also, a $\bar{\mathsf{\tau}}_{\mathsf{U}_{2}\mathsf{I}\mathsf{C O O}\mathsf{I}_{4}}$ cluster based MOF with urea group on the framework was studied in converting ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ to corresponding cyclic carbonate, which exhibited remarkably catalytic activity.[77]
Next, the $N{\dot{\mathsf{I}}}_{2}$ metal cluster was also used to construct MOF catalysts for ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ cycloaddition. For example, Duan’s group[78] constructed a single-walled MOF Ni-TCPE1 for the cycloaddition of carbon dioxide by using tetrakis(4-carboxyphenyl)ethylene $(H_{4}\mathsf{T C P E})$ as the ligand. Single crystal X-ray analysis revealed that Ni−TCPE1 crystallizes in the P-3 space group. Two carboxylate groups and one water molecule bridge two nickel ions to form a $N{\dot{\mathsf{I}}}_{2}$ cluster. The $N{\dot{\mathsf{I}}}_{2}$ cluster shows a similar Lewis acidity similar to $\mathsf{C u}_{2}$ cluster. Thus, a high yield of $99\%$ was obtained in cycloaddition of ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ with styrene oxide under $373\mathsf{K}$ and 10 atm.
Compared with the $Z n_{4}O$ cluster, $\boldsymbol{\mathsf{M}}_{2}$ cluster-based MOFs showed higher activity toward ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ cycloaddition. However, cocatalysts still need to be introduced into the reaction system to accelerate the catalytic process.
## 2.1.2.3. $z r_{6}0_{8}$ cluster
UIO (University of Oslo) series MOFs consist of $Z r_{6}O_{8}$ metal clusters and linear dicarboxylic acid ligands. The $Z r_{6}O_{8}$ metal cluster usually presents twelve-coordinated connections, in which each $Z r_{4}$ is linked to four $\mu_{3}–0^{2\cdot}$ and four carboxylic acid oxygen, respectively, forming an octadecahedron configuration. Note, the two water molecules of nodes within UIO-type MOFs can be removed under high temperature, thereby becoming $Z r_{6}O_{6}$ clusters with potential Lewis acid catalytic activity.[79] In 2016, Liu et al.[80] developed a metal organogel material based on UIO- $66\substack{-N H_{2}}$ nanoparticles (Figure 5). The results showed that the organic gel exhibited the high efficiency for converting ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ to cyclic carbonate. Compared with the conventional UIO-66- $N H_{2}$ microcrystalline, MOF gel showed higher activity due to their larger surface area and high concentration of defect sites in the MOF gel. In addition, the gel catalyst can be reused for five cycles.
