## 2.1.3. Dual metal catalytic sites
Since Lewis acid is mainly catalytic sites for ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ cycloaddition. herefore, an efficient way to enhance catalytic activity is to duce the extra Lewis acid sites in MOFs. Sorts of strategies including the usage of organometallic ligands, macrocyclic ligands, and heterometallic nodes, etc. were developed to construct catalysts for $\mathsf{C O}_{2}$ cycloaddition. Metalloporphyrin ligands inherently possess the metal chelating sites on their molecules. herefore, the MOF materials with these ligands may exhibit dual Lewis acid sites with adjustable functions. For example, in 2013, Ren et al.[88] synthesized a Ni(salphen) ligand-based 3D Cd-MOF [ $C d_{2}(N i\mathrm{-L})_{2}(H_{2}O)_{4}].$ 3DMF via the $H_{2}L$ 1((E)-3-(3-tert-butyl-5-fomyl-4-hydroxyphenyl)acrylic acid), $N i(O A c)_{2}\cdot4H_{2}O$ , and ${\mathsf{C d C l}}_{2}$ etc, with a one-dimensional pore (Figure 8). Single crystal structure analysis showed that $\mathsf{N i}^{2+}$ in salen ligand present the planar square configuration and can serve as potential Lewis acidity sites. Ni(salphen) ligand is linked $.0$ two $\mathsf{C d}_{2}$ clusters to generate a porous 2D network. Thus, the $\mathsf{C d}_{2}$ cluster can also be another kind of Lewis sites together with $\mathsf{N i}^{2+}$ sites to synergistic activation of reactants. The optimized
yield of $86\%$ can be obtained under mild conditions of $100^{\circ}\mathsf C$ and 20 atm.
In 2017, Ren’s group[89] designed and used another Ni(salphen) ligand to construct a 3D chiral MOF, $[(\mathsf{C u}_{4}\mathsf{l}_{4})_{2}\mathsf{L}_{4}]\cdot20\mathsf{D M F}\cdot3\mathsf{C H}_{3}\mathsf{C N}$ (1) [L is (R, R)-N,N'-bis(3-tert-butyl-5-(4-pyridyl)salicylidene)-1,2-diphenylethy lenediamine nickel(II)]. The Ni(salphen) ligands link two $C u_{4}l_{4}$ clusters with a 4-connected tetrahedral configuration to form a dia topology 3D network with two types of hydrophobic channels. Note, Ni(salen) moieties of ligands lie inside of 1D channels and the empty coordination sites of $\mathsf{N i}^{2+}$ orient to the cavities. Moreover, compound 1 exhibited good chemical stability and thermal stability. An extra high yield of $99\%$ was achieved toward the synthesis of chloropropene carbonate, which can be attributed to its high ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ capture ability as well as the synergistic Lewis acidic activation of high-density Ni(salen) units in 1D channels. In 2018, Cao et al.[90] developed a strategy to prepare bifunctional multivariate Zr-MOFs $(Z\mathsf{n}\mathsf{T C P P}\mathsf{C}(\mathsf{B r}^{-})$ Etim-UiO-66) by incorporating zinc porphyrin and imidazolium functionalized groups into MOFs (Scheme 9). $Z\mathsf{n T C P P C}(\mathsf{B r^{-}})$ Etim-UiO-66 can catalyze the cycloaddition of epichlorohydrin with ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ to form the chloropropene carbonate with a yield of $86.9\%$ . The catalyst can perform for four cycles. The synergistic effect was observed in catalyzing a series of epoxides into cyclic carbonate under a cocatalyst-free condition, in which the $Z n^{2+}$ center in porphyrin ligand acts as a Lewis acid catalyst, the $B r$ on the imidazolate ligand acts as a Lewis base.
