## 3.2.1.2. Conversion of $\mathbf{co}_{2}$ to syngas
Beside CO, some small-molecule gases, such as $C H_{4}$ and ${\mathsf{C}}_{2}{\mathsf{H}}_{4},$ could be obtained by MOF electrocatalysts. In 2018, Eddaoudi group[176] fabricated MOF thin films on gold nanostructured microelectrodes (AuNMEs) via layer-by-layer method and in situ solvothermal method (Figure 26). The results showed that the MOF thin films are capable of completely suppressing CO production and producing detectable quantities of $C H_{4}$ and $C_{2}H_{4}$ . This study proved the use of MOF thin films to tune the activity of an underlying $C O_{2}R R$ catalyst to produce further-reduced products. However, the modest electrical conductivity and weak rate of charge transfer result in low activity, which may be a common problem for most MOFs.
In 2019, Guntern et al.[177] combined Ag nanocrystals (NCs) with Al-PMOF $[\mathsf{A l}_{2}({\mathsf{O H}})_{2}(\mathsf{T C P P})]$ $\textstyle\left({\mathsf{T C P P}}=\right.$ tetrakis(4-carboxyphenyl)porphyrin)) to form Ag@Al-PMOF hybrids (Scheme 19). The Faradic efficiencies (FEs) of the Ag@Al-PMOF and bare ${\sf A}{\sf g}$ NCs with different thicknesses were tested in 0.1 M $K{\mathsf{H C O}}_{3}$ and $0.5\mathsf{M K H C O}_{3},$ respectively. Moreover, the results showed that with the increase of the thickness of the MOF layer, there is a decrease in hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) and an increase in the CO production at higher buffer capacity, since the higher local pH suppresses the HER process. On the other hand, at lower buffer capacity, there is no obvious distinction in the FEs between two thicknesses. This suggests that electronic effects can be also an impact factor. In addition, the morphological stability of the Ag NCs is also increased when combined with the Al-PMOF. Most importantly, this work provides a new strategy to rationally design electrocatalytic materials with remarkable selectivity and stability.
